const e="namcya-national-music-competitions-young-artists",c=2026,n="Read: NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines (15 pages; pages 1 and 2 are cover pages) and the ten 2026 category guidelines, plus the 2025 General Guidelines and category guidelines (37 pages). The template cites the 2025 edition, but the 2026 edition is now current (the template's own Url points at the 2026 page). The page-wide rules, dates, fees and contacts are therefore the 2026 values and are Variables. The 2026 edition changed the class list: only Traditional Music Expressions exists in both, so that row uses the 2026 text. The template's other classes (Children's Solo Rondalla, Junior Guitar, Junior Rondalla, Children's Choir, Senior Choir, Symphonic Band, Senior Piano, Senior Strings, Senior Lower Strings, Senior Voice, Woodwinds) are not in 2026, so their rows and age-group rows carry the 2025 edition rules and are marked 2025 edition. The 2026 classes the template does not carry are one short line each under page key other (age, group size and judging criteria). Not copied: the bank account number printed in the 2026 guidelines (only the payment method is kept); the full 2026 repertoire lists of the 2026 category guidelines (Senior Guitar, Junior Piano, Junior Strings, Brass, Junior Voice), which are classes the template does not carry, and the cello and contrabass recommended lists of the 2025 strings guidelines; the 2025 edition dates and application deadlines (superseded). The 2026 guidelines print no cash prize amounts and no mark bands. The 2025 Senior Choir age is 18 to 30 as printed, while the template's Senior Choir group starts at 18 too; the Junior Rondalla 2025 range is 13 to 18.",o=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"NAMCYA - National Music Competitions for Young Artists. Read these rules before you register.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"NAMCYA 2026: send your intent-to-join form during {{IntentToJoinWindow}}, your documents by {{ApplicationDocsDeadline}} and your video and scores by {{VideoScoresDeadline}}. Questions go only to {{ApplicationsEmail}}.","Notes":["Dates and venues may change. The NAMCYA Secretariat releases official updates.","Ages are counted on {{AgeCutoffDate}} in the 2026 edition.","Only the persons whose names are in the official list may appear in the audition video. Anyone else appearing is a ground for automatic disqualification and for taking back all awards, distinctions and prizes."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"About NAMCYA","Items":["NAMCYA began under Presidential Proclamation No. 1173 and is now in Republic Act No. 11915. It is the national music development program of the Philippines for young musicians and ensembles.","NAMCYA 2026 is the 53rd NAMCYA (Padayaw 2026).","Vision: to be the main agent in the advancement and fostering of the diverse musical culture and heritage of the Philippines and in the development of outstanding young Filipino musicians.","Mission: to identify outstanding young Filipino musicians through competitions, and to develop them to be ambassadors of Philippine musical culture and heritage.","2026 classes: Senior Guitar, Junior Voice, Junior Piano, Junior Strings and Lower Strings, Brass, Youth Choir (Mixed and Equal Voices), Junior Solo Rondalla Instrument, Children's Rondalla, Traditional Music Expressions and Contemporary Music Ensemble (special category).","Solo classes: Junior Solo Rondalla Instrument, Senior Guitar, Junior Strings and Lower Strings, Junior Piano, Junior Voice and Brass. Group classes: Youth Choir and Children's Rondalla. Special classes: Traditional Music Expressions and Contemporary Music Ensemble.","Follow the official repertoire rules of each class. Works are performed from memory unless the class rules say otherwise.","Time is counted from the first note or movement to the last cut-off. Follow the time limit of the class strictly.","Time over the limit loses points: 30 seconds over, 0.5 point off the total score of each judge. 1 minute over, 1 point. 1 minute 30 seconds over, 2 points. 2 to 5 minutes over, 5 points or possible disqualification, as the class rules say.","The levels are the Elimination Level (screening and selection of semifinal qualifiers), the Regional Cluster Level (semifinals for NCR, Northern Luzon, Southern Luzon, Visayas and Mindanao) and the National Level (finals in Metro Manila venues such as CCP, Metropolitan Theater, NMP and Luneta).","Safety and welfare: follow the safety rules and emergency steps of every venue. NAMCYA is not liable for lost instruments, valuables or personal belongings. Keep your things safe and label your instruments.","Attendance: arrive at least one hour before your scheduled performance and soundcheck or rehearsal. A late person may be disqualified or may have to perform out of competition, and the rehearsal slot may be lost, at the choice of the Artistic and Program Director.","Stage behavior: bow politely before and after your performance.","Instruments: bring all instruments and accessories that you need. Instruments must be tuned and ready before call time."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Who May Enter","Items":["You must be a Filipino citizen within the age range of your class on {{AgeCutoffDate}}.","Earlier NAMCYA winners may join again only where the class rules allow it (for example a higher division or a new ensemble).","You must represent a school, conservatory, institution, local government unit or community-based organisation.","Winning international competitions does not count against you. Groups and persons who won international competitions may enter NAMCYA if they follow all rules.","Only the persons whose names are in the official list may appear in the audition video. Anyone else appearing is a ground for automatic disqualification and for taking back all awards, distinctions and prizes.","You may represent only one institution or ensemble in each class.","Giving false information about age, repertoire or membership means automatic disqualification.","Each class has its own age range, group size and rules. See the class rows below."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Step 1: send the intent-to-join form during {{IntentToJoinWindow}} (Google form).","Step 2: you receive a confirmation and detailed instructions, with a Google Drive link to upload your video, scores and other documents.","Step 3: send the application documents by {{ApplicationDocsDeadline}} and the audition video and scores by {{VideoScoresDeadline}} (Google forms). Traditional Music Expressions sends its video by {{TMEVideoDeadline}}.","When your submission is complete, you receive a certificate that your entry is accepted for adjudication. You are told whether your submission is accepted for adjudication or not.","Application documents: the intent-to-join form, the audition video, a high-resolution photo, a scanned birth certificate for every competitor and conductor, the Repertoire Form for each class and level, and the music scores.","Audition video: the preferred format is MP4. Use a single camera. A phone or camera on a tripod in landscape mode gives better quality.","The video must be recorded for the 2026 competition, with a date stamp not earlier than {{VideoDateStampFrom}}.","The video must have no cuts, editing, zooming or panning, and no audio enhancement.","Name the video file with your name or group name and the estimated performance time, for example namcyachorale_4.50.","Strings: the face, both arms, the whole bow and the instrument must be clearly seen. The instrument must be properly tuned. A video with an untuned instrument is disqualified.","Piano: the face and hands must be seen all the time.","Music scores: send clear PDF copies of the scores of your repertoire. Name each file Composer_Title_ContestantLastName_Category, for example FredericChopin_SonataOp.35_DelaCruz_JuniorPiano.","The score PDFs must include the permission of the composer or publisher, except for public domain works.","In the semifinal and national finals rounds, hand in three copies of each piece (not the contest piece, which NAMCYA provides) in a white folder for the three adjudicators.","Entries that do not follow the requirements are rejected and the applicant is told.","Sending an entry means you accept the competition rules fully.","Technical problems or other concerns: write to {{ApplicationsEmail}}. NAMCYA does not answer inquiries, concerns or messages sent anywhere else and is not liable for missed emails or messages sent to another account.","Change of repertoire after you submit: write to {{ApplicationsEmail}} two weeks before the scheduled competition. The Chairman of the class decides. You need written approval from NAMCYA to avoid disqualification.","Change of the list of members of a group after you submit: write to {{ApplicationsEmail}} two weeks before the scheduled competition. The Chairman of the class decides. The group needs written approval from NAMCYA to avoid disqualification.","Changes or substitutions of persons after you submit must be approved formally by the NAMCYA Secretariat."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Registration Fee","Items":["The registration fee is {{SoloFee}}.","For group classes the registration fee is {{GroupFee}}.","The fee is paid by deposit to the bank account of the NAMCYA Foundation: over the counter or by online bank transfer.","GCash payments (GCash to the NAMCYA bank account) are not accepted.","Write the name of the applicant or the group name in the reference number or payor's name line."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Important Dates","Items":["Intent-to-join form: {{IntentToJoinWindow}}.","Application documents: by {{ApplicationDocsDeadline}}.","Video and scores: by {{VideoScoresDeadline}}. Traditional Music Expressions video: by {{TMEVideoDeadline}}.","Elimination round (via Zoom): {{EliminationRoundDates}}. Traditional Music Expressions video elimination (via Zoom): {{TMEEliminationDate}}.","Mindanao Cluster semifinal: {{MindanaoSemifinal}}.","Visayas Cluster semifinal: {{VisayasSemifinal}}.","Northern Luzon Cluster semifinal: {{NorthernLuzonSemifinal}}.","Southern Luzon Cluster semifinal: {{SouthernLuzonSemifinal}}.","National Capital Region Cluster semifinal: {{NCRSemifinal}}.","Solo semifinals: {{SoloSemifinals}}.","National Finals Week: {{NationalFinalsDates}}.","Some dates and venues are tentative and may change. The NAMCYA Secretariat releases official updates."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue","Items":["The National Finals are held at {{FinalsVenue}}. Finals are held in Metro Manila venues.","Semifinal venues are in the Dates section. The NAMCYA office is at {{SecretariatAddress}}."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Rounds and Qualification","Items":["Elimination Level: all entries are judged by the assigned adjudicators. The adjudicators decide how many go to the semifinals.","Regional Cluster Level: the number that go on depends on the quality of the performances and the advice of the adjudicators.","Solo classes, semifinal round: the adjudicators decide how many go to the finals, unless the class rules say a number.","National Level: finals in Metro Manila.","A contest piece may or may not be needed in a class. If it is, the announcement comes after the semifinal round."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging","Items":["The jury is a specially convened panel that includes industry professionals. Each class has at least three adjudicators appointed by the class chairperson.","The scoring criteria differ by class. See the class rows.","Marks are added up by staff appointed by NAMCYA under the Chief Adjudicator. Tied scores may be settled by discussion or by weighting criteria.","Judges may write feedback for learning, but they may not talk about results with contestants during or after the competition.","Jury talks for the elimination round begin on {{EliminationRoundDates}}, and the qualifiers of each class are announced soon after judging. NAMCYA may change the schedule for unforeseen reasons.","The judges' choice of qualifiers is final. No messages or feedback about the panel's decision are allowed. Emails asking for feedback are not passed on to the panel.","The decision of the judges is final and binding.","Extraordinary cases during the competition go to the panel of judges and the artistic director for discussion.","NAMCYA does not discriminate by race, color, religion (creed), gender, gender expression, age, national origin or ancestry, disability, marital status, sexual orientation or military status."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Order of Performance and Other Rules","Items":["The order of performance is decided by a drawing of lots (via Zoom) and stays the same through the competition.","Accompanists: only registered accompanists may play. You must bring your own accompanist. Only one accompanist is allowed for the whole performance.","An accompanist may help more than one contestant but must not disturb NAMCYA's schedule. Unauthorized substitutions must be reported to the secretariat.","You must get your own instruments for the performances.","You must get permission to perform copyrighted works.","Failure to follow, or falsifying, any requirement is a sufficient ground for disqualification."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Prizes and Recognition","Items":["National awards, if funds in the approved budget and sponsorship allow: First Prize, Second Prize and Third Prize.","In the National Finals a class may have no winner. No First Prize or Second Prize may be given. An Honorable Mention may be given, at the choice of the Board of Adjudicators, depending on the quality of the finalists.","All participants receive a Certificate of Recognition from NAMCYA. Teachers, conductors and accompanists also receive Certificates of Recognition.","Certificates of Appearance are issued only after the competition ends. Each person or group must collect them in person from the secretariat.","The 2026 guidelines print no cash prize amounts."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct","Items":["Show discipline, respect and humility at all times.","Coaches act as mentors. They are not negotiators or advocates during the competition.","Attire for soloists: formal barong or Filipiniana, or concert black, with formal shoes. Attire for ensembles: uniform or coordinated clothes.","Clothes inspired by culture are encouraged in the traditional and folk classes.","Posting negative or defamatory remarks about adjudicators, other contestants and NAMCYA personnel on social media is strictly forbidden.","NAMCYA may withdraw awards from participants found guilty of misconduct."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Complaints","Items":["Send any concern to NAMCYA in writing on the same competition day.","In an extraordinary case, results may be suspended for a while during an investigation.","The decision of the NAMCYA Artistic and Program Director, after review, is final."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other 2026 Classes and Notes","Items":["Junior Solo Rondalla Instrument (2026): ages 13 to 19 on {{AgeCutoffDate}}. Judging: technical 30, musicality 30, interpretation and style 20, coherence with the accompanist 20. One guitar accompanist only.","Senior Guitar (2026): ages 19 to 30 on {{AgeCutoffDate}}. Judging: technical proficiency 30, musical interpretation 30, overall artistic impression 40.","Junior Piano (2026): up to 19 years on {{AgeCutoffDate}}. Judging: technical mastery 30, musical interpretation 30, overall artistic impression 30, repertoire selection 10.","Junior Strings and Lower Strings (2026, violin, viola, cello, contrabass): up to 19 years on {{AgeCutoffDate}}. Judging: technical proficiency 30, musical interpretation 30, overall performance 40.","Junior Voice (2026): up to 19 years on {{AgeCutoffDate}}. No voice-type divisions. Judging: vocal technique 50, artistry 50.","Brass (2026, High Brass and Low Brass): ages 19 to 30 on {{AgeCutoffDate}}. Judging: technical proficiency 50, musicality 50.","Youth Choir, Mixed and Equal Voices (2026): singers 13 to 19 years on {{AgeCutoffDate}}, 16 to 24 singers, one conductor. Judging: technical proficiency 30, musical interpretation 25, ensemble cohesion 25, repertoire selection 10, overall artistic expression 10.","Children's Rondalla (2026): members up to 14 years on {{AgeCutoffDate}}, 10 to 20 members and one conductor. Judging: technical proficiency 25, musicality 25, interpretation and style 25, ensemble cohesion 25.","Contemporary Music Ensemble, special category, new in 2026: open to participants up to 32 years old, 3 to 8 performers, elimination 4 to 6 minutes, semifinal and final up to 12 minutes each.","The 2025 classes Senior Piano, Senior Strings, Senior Lower Strings, Senior Voice A and B, Woodwinds (Open), Junior Guitar, Senior Choir, Children's Choir, Junior Rondalla, Children's Solo Rondalla and Symphonic Band are not in the 2026 list. Their rows below are marked 2025 edition."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"2026 General Guidelines","Url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Kzz7WvnTwrxtE6-TJj3hcyoOhECzuWoQ/view"},{"Title":"2026 Traditional Music Expressions guidelines","Url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kcC5aF3D72-t7qyIjS5Zbro-VJfHj8e5/view"},{"Title":"2026 category guidelines and application links (Linktree)","Url":"https://linktr.ee/socmed.namcya"},{"Title":"2026 competitions and guidelines page","Url":"https://www.namcya.com/comptetition/2026-namcya-competitions-and-guidelines/"}]}`),i=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines VI 3a, IX 2a, IX 5",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Send a 2x2 photo (300 dpi). Save the file as lastname_category.jpg.","Soloists wear formal barong or Filipiniana, or concert black, with formal shoes.","Soloists bring their own accompanist."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Send a 2x2 photo (300 dpi). Save the file as lastname_category.jpg.
- Soloists wear formal barong or Filipiniana, or concert black, with formal shoes.
- Soloists bring their own accompanist.`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines VI 3a, VI 4, IX 2a",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Send one 4R group photo and one 2x2 photo (300 dpi) of each group member, including the conductor. Save each file as lastname_category.jpg.","Send a scanned birth certificate for each member and the conductor.","Groups wear a uniform or coordinated clothes.","The registration fee for a group class is {{GroupFee}}."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Send one 4R group photo and one 2x2 photo (300 dpi) of each group member, including the conductor. Save each file as lastname_category.jpg.
- Send a scanned birth certificate for each member and the conductor.
- Groups wear a uniform or coordinated clothes.
- The registration fee for a group class is {{GroupFee}}.`}],t=[{AgeGroup:"Children Solo",Source:"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Children's Solo Rondalla I",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["2025 edition: the contestant must not be older than 12 years by December 31, 2025."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 2025 edition: the contestant must not be older than 12 years by December 31, 2025.`},{AgeGroup:"Children Choir",Source:"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Children's Choir I",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["2025 edition: singers must be 14 years old or younger by December 31, 2025."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 2025 edition: singers must be 14 years old or younger by December 31, 2025.`},{AgeGroup:"Junior Solo",Source:"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Junior Guitar I",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["2025 edition: the contestant must be 13 to 18 years old by December 31, 2025."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 2025 edition: the contestant must be 13 to 18 years old by December 31, 2025.`},{AgeGroup:"Junior Rondalla",Source:"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Junior Rondalla I",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["2025 edition: members must be at least 13 and not more than 18 years old by December 31, 2025."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 2025 edition: members must be at least 13 and not more than 18 years old by December 31, 2025.`},{AgeGroup:"Senior Choir",Source:"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Senior Choir I",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["2025 edition: singers must be 18 to 30 years old by December 31, 2025."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 2025 edition: singers must be 18 to 30 years old by December 31, 2025.`},{AgeGroup:"Senior Solo",Source:"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Senior Piano, Senior Strings, Woodwinds (Open) I",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["2025 edition: piano, strings and woodwinds contestants must be 19 to 30 years old by December 31, 2025."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 2025 edition: piano, strings and woodwinds contestants must be 19 to 30 years old by December 31, 2025.`},{AgeGroup:"Senior Voice A",Source:"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Senior Voice I",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["2025 edition: ages 19 to 24 years as of December 31, 2025."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 2025 edition: ages 19 to 24 years as of December 31, 2025.`},{AgeGroup:"Senior Voice B",Source:"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Senior Voice I",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["2025 edition: ages 25 to 31 years as of December 31, 2025."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 2025 edition: ages 25 to 31 years as of December 31, 2025.`},{AgeGroup:"Symphonic Band",Source:"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Symphonic Band 1.1",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["2025 edition: members must be not more than 23 years old by December 31, 2025. The Conductor and Assistant Conductor are exempt from the age rule."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 2025 edition: members must be not more than 23 years old by December 31, 2025. The Conductor and Assistant Conductor are exempt from the age rule.`},{AgeGroup:"Traditional",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 Traditional Music Expressions guidelines I, II",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Each performance must prominently feature at least one member who is no more than 18 years old on {{AgeCutoffDate}}. There is no printed age limit for the other members."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Each performance must prominently feature at least one member who is no more than 18 years old on {{AgeCutoffDate}}. There is no printed age limit for the other members.`}],a=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Children's Solo Rondalla","Source":"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Children's Solo Rondalla","Sections":{"About":["2025 edition: a solo class for rondalla instruments."],"TimeAndFormat":["Semifinal: total playing time up to 10 minutes. The order of the pieces is the contestant's choice."],"Rules":["Video elimination: one foreign or Filipino piece. It may be a folk song or an original piece arranged or composed for a solo rondalla instrument.","Semifinal: one Filipino piece and one foreign piece that were not played in the elimination round. Show a variety of styles.","National Finals: one piece of choice that was played in the elimination or semifinal round, and one contest piece. Finalists get a copy of the contest piece within five business days after the last semifinal.","You may play unaccompanied or with accompaniment. If accompanied, only one guitarist is allowed.","The pieces must be written or arranged for solo rondalla. Send a copy of the score to NAMCYA."],"Allowed":["Only the accompanist may read sheet music."],"NotAllowed":["The solo contestant may not use sheet music. All pieces are played from memory."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["Dress in a way that is decent, age-appropriate and comfortable."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- 2025 edition: a solo class for rondalla instruments.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Semifinal: total playing time up to 10 minutes. The order of the pieces is the contestant's choice.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Video elimination: one foreign or Filipino piece. It may be a folk song or an original piece arranged or composed for a solo rondalla instrument.\\n- Semifinal: one Filipino piece and one foreign piece that were not played in the elimination round. Show a variety of styles.\\n- National Finals: one piece of choice that was played in the elimination or semifinal round, and one contest piece. Finalists get a copy of the contest piece within five business days after the last semifinal.\\n- You may play unaccompanied or with accompaniment. If accompanied, only one guitarist is allowed.\\n- The pieces must be written or arranged for solo rondalla. Send a copy of the score to NAMCYA.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Only the accompanist may read sheet music.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- The solo contestant may not use sheet music. All pieces are played from memory.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Dress in a way that is decent, age-appropriate and comfortable."},{"Title":"Junior Guitar","Source":"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Junior Guitar","Sections":{"About":["2025 edition: a solo guitar class."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Video elimination, three required studies: Study Op. 38 No. 3 by Napoleon Coste, Study Op. 31 No. 19 by Fernando Sor, Study Op. 48 No. 5 by Mauro Giuliani.","Semifinal, free choice: one Renaissance piece originally written for the lute or vihuela (2 to 4 minutes). Suggested composers are John Dowland, Francis Cutting, Thomas Campion, Anthony Holborne, Robert Johnson, Philip Rosseter, Luis Milan, Alonso Mudarra, Luis de Narvaez and Miguel de Fuenllana. You may use the original vihuela tablature with the third string tuned to F sharp.","Semifinal: one movement or a paired movement from the Six Cello Suites or Five Lute Suites of J.S. Bach (paired movements such as Gavotte I and II from BWV 995, and Gigue and Double from BWV 997, are allowed).","Semifinal: one etude or work from the collections Estudios Sencillos and Nuevos Estudios Sencillos by Leo Brouwer, Etudes Esquisses by Gerald Garcia, Album de la Inocencia by Eduardo Martin, or 14 Etudes by Maximo Diego Pujol.","National Finals: play works from all three groups. First, one 19th century piece originally written for guitar, from a suggested composer (Giulio Regondi, Napoleon Coste, Dionisio Aguado, Luigi Legnani, Julian Arcas, Johann Kaspar Mertz, Francisco Tarrega, Miguel Llobet, Agustin Barrios Mangore) or another composer of the same period or style.","National Finals: second, one fast piece or fast movement written for guitar in the 20th or 21st century, 4 to 8 minutes. In a work with several movements, play one or two movements.","National Finals: third, one required Filipino original guitar work: Batikusan or Kapilas na Giting by Bayani Mendoza de Leon, Prelude Etnika by Lucrecia Kasilag, Panagimpan by Jose Valdez, Harana or the Prelude and Fugue by Angel Pena, or Manang Biday by Florante Aguilar.","All pieces must be played from memory."],"Allowed":["A modern classical guitar."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- 2025 edition: a solo guitar class.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Video elimination, three required studies: Study Op. 38 No. 3 by Napoleon Coste, Study Op. 31 No. 19 by Fernando Sor, Study Op. 48 No. 5 by Mauro Giuliani.\\n- Semifinal, free choice: one Renaissance piece originally written for the lute or vihuela (2 to 4 minutes). Suggested composers are John Dowland, Francis Cutting, Thomas Campion, Anthony Holborne, Robert Johnson, Philip Rosseter, Luis Milan, Alonso Mudarra, Luis de Narvaez and Miguel de Fuenllana. You may use the original vihuela tablature with the third string tuned to F sharp.\\n- Semifinal: one movement or a paired movement from the Six Cello Suites or Five Lute Suites of J.S. Bach (paired movements such as Gavotte I and II from BWV 995, and Gigue and Double from BWV 997, are allowed).\\n- Semifinal: one etude or work from the collections Estudios Sencillos and Nuevos Estudios Sencillos by Leo Brouwer, Etudes Esquisses by Gerald Garcia, Album de la Inocencia by Eduardo Martin, or 14 Etudes by Maximo Diego Pujol.\\n- National Finals: play works from all three groups. First, one 19th century piece originally written for guitar, from a suggested composer (Giulio Regondi, Napoleon Coste, Dionisio Aguado, Luigi Legnani, Julian Arcas, Johann Kaspar Mertz, Francisco Tarrega, Miguel Llobet, Agustin Barrios Mangore) or another composer of the same period or style.\\n- National Finals: second, one fast piece or fast movement written for guitar in the 20th or 21st century, 4 to 8 minutes. In a work with several movements, play one or two movements.\\n- National Finals: third, one required Filipino original guitar work: Batikusan or Kapilas na Giting by Bayani Mendoza de Leon, Prelude Etnika by Lucrecia Kasilag, Panagimpan by Jose Valdez, Harana or the Prelude and Fugue by Angel Pena, or Manang Biday by Florante Aguilar.\\n- All pieces must be played from memory.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- A modern classical guitar."},{"Title":"Junior Rondalla","Source":"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Junior Rondalla","Sections":{"About":["2025 edition: a group class for school, church, family or community rondallas."],"TimeAndFormat":["Semifinal: total playing time up to 10 minutes. The order of the pieces is the group's choice."],"Rules":["The group has 12 to 20 performing members and one conductor.","The conductor and the members may play with only one group in the competition.","Video elimination: one foreign or Filipino piece. It may be a folk song or an original piece arranged or composed for rondalla instruments.","Semifinal: two pieces, one Filipino and one foreign, different from the elimination round.","National Finals: one piece of choice played in the elimination or semifinal round, and one contest piece. Finalists get a copy of the contest piece within five business days after the last semifinal.","The pieces must be composed or arranged for rondalla, with a score that shows the instruments as played. Send a copy of the score to NAMCYA.","The members and the conductor play all pieces from memory, without scores or sheet music.","The seating layout for the stage shown in the guidelines must be followed. Only small changes, such as seat distance, are allowed."],"Allowed":["Choreography and movements that are part of the basic structure of a piece (hand clapping, head swaying, foot stomping, body percussion) if the composer or arranger asks for them."],"NotAllowed":["Transposition or any other version of the contest piece.","Drums or a drum set in the semifinals and finals."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["Dress in a way that is decent, age-appropriate and comfortable."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- 2025 edition: a group class for school, church, family or community rondallas.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Semifinal: total playing time up to 10 minutes. The order of the pieces is the group's choice.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The group has 12 to 20 performing members and one conductor.\\n- The conductor and the members may play with only one group in the competition.\\n- Video elimination: one foreign or Filipino piece. It may be a folk song or an original piece arranged or composed for rondalla instruments.\\n- Semifinal: two pieces, one Filipino and one foreign, different from the elimination round.\\n- National Finals: one piece of choice played in the elimination or semifinal round, and one contest piece. Finalists get a copy of the contest piece within five business days after the last semifinal.\\n- The pieces must be composed or arranged for rondalla, with a score that shows the instruments as played. Send a copy of the score to NAMCYA.\\n- The members and the conductor play all pieces from memory, without scores or sheet music.\\n- The seating layout for the stage shown in the guidelines must be followed. Only small changes, such as seat distance, are allowed.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Choreography and movements that are part of the basic structure of a piece (hand clapping, head swaying, foot stomping, body percussion) if the composer or arranger asks for them.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Transposition or any other version of the contest piece.\\n- Drums or a drum set in the semifinals and finals.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Dress in a way that is decent, age-appropriate and comfortable."},{"Title":"Children's Choir","Source":"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Children's Choir","Sections":{"About":["2025 edition: a group class for school, church, cultural, civic or community children's choirs."],"TimeAndFormat":["Video elimination: two pieces from the existing repertoire, preferably in contrasting styles, total singing time up to 9 minutes (not counting entrance, pause and exit).","Semifinal: total singing time up to 12 minutes.","National Finals: total singing time up to 15 minutes."],"Rules":["The class is for real members of the school, church, cultural, civic or community that the choir represents. All singers must be Filipino citizens aged 14 or younger by December 31, 2025.","A choir has 16 to 24 singers, one accompanist and one conductor. Other instrumentalists needed in a piece must come from within the choir.","Members may sing with only one group at all levels. The conductor may perform with another group only in another class.","Video elimination: at least one piece must be a cappella. The recording must be live (not a virtual choir) and the sound must not be changed by technology. It must begin with a short introduction of the choir's name, the conductor's name and the titles and composers or arrangers of the pieces. No cuts.","Semifinal: one piece by a non-Filipino composer, one Philippine choral work in the original language (preferably from the choir's region), and one piece of choice not sung in the video elimination. At least two pieces are sung a cappella.","National Finals: one piece by a non-Filipino composer and one original piece by a Filipino composer, neither sung before, and the obligatory piece (given out after the semifinals). At least one piece is a cappella.","Pieces may not be repeated at any level.","The choir sings in the key written in the score.","Send PDF scores of the video elimination pieces with the general packet. The last date for pieces is 15 days before the date of the elimination, semifinal and final rounds. Pieces cannot be changed after submission.","The PDFs must have the permission of the composer or publisher, except for public domain pieces."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Three expert judges. Technical merit 50 percent and artistic merit 50 percent.","Technical: overall sound quality, steady intonation, accurate rhythm, width of dynamic range, correct harmony and proper diction.","Artistic: musicality (expression, interpretation and style, tone, balance and blend) and programming (choice of pieces, presentation, faithfulness to the score, variety, difficulty and suitability to the choir).","Time over the limit: 1 point for each minute. 1 to 30 seconds over is 0.5 point. More than 30 seconds is 1 full point."],"Points":["First, Second and Third prizes are given in the national finals. A prize may be left out if the jury finds the choirs below the technical and artistic standard.","The jury may give other special awards."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- 2025 edition: a group class for school, church, cultural, civic or community children's choirs.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Video elimination: two pieces from the existing repertoire, preferably in contrasting styles, total singing time up to 9 minutes (not counting entrance, pause and exit).\\n- Semifinal: total singing time up to 12 minutes.\\n- National Finals: total singing time up to 15 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The class is for real members of the school, church, cultural, civic or community that the choir represents. All singers must be Filipino citizens aged 14 or younger by December 31, 2025.\\n- A choir has 16 to 24 singers, one accompanist and one conductor. Other instrumentalists needed in a piece must come from within the choir.\\n- Members may sing with only one group at all levels. The conductor may perform with another group only in another class.\\n- Video elimination: at least one piece must be a cappella. The recording must be live (not a virtual choir) and the sound must not be changed by technology. It must begin with a short introduction of the choir's name, the conductor's name and the titles and composers or arrangers of the pieces. No cuts.\\n- Semifinal: one piece by a non-Filipino composer, one Philippine choral work in the original language (preferably from the choir's region), and one piece of choice not sung in the video elimination. At least two pieces are sung a cappella.\\n- National Finals: one piece by a non-Filipino composer and one original piece by a Filipino composer, neither sung before, and the obligatory piece (given out after the semifinals). At least one piece is a cappella.\\n- Pieces may not be repeated at any level.\\n- The choir sings in the key written in the score.\\n- Send PDF scores of the video elimination pieces with the general packet. The last date for pieces is 15 days before the date of the elimination, semifinal and final rounds. Pieces cannot be changed after submission.\\n- The PDFs must have the permission of the composer or publisher, except for public domain pieces.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Three expert judges. Technical merit 50 percent and artistic merit 50 percent.\\n- Technical: overall sound quality, steady intonation, accurate rhythm, width of dynamic range, correct harmony and proper diction.\\n- Artistic: musicality (expression, interpretation and style, tone, balance and blend) and programming (choice of pieces, presentation, faithfulness to the score, variety, difficulty and suitability to the choir).\\n- Time over the limit: 1 point for each minute. 1 to 30 seconds over is 0.5 point. More than 30 seconds is 1 full point.\\n\\n## Points\\n- First, Second and Third prizes are given in the national finals. A prize may be left out if the jury finds the choirs below the technical and artistic standard.\\n- The jury may give other special awards."},{"Title":"Senior Choir","Source":"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Senior Choir","Sections":{"About":["2025 edition: a group class for school, church, cultural, civic or community choirs, mixed or equal voices."],"TimeAndFormat":["Video elimination: singing time up to 9 minutes (not counting entrance, pause and exit).","Semifinal: up to 12 minutes.","National Finals: up to 15 minutes."],"Rules":["Singers must be Filipino citizens, 18 to 30 years old by December 31, 2025, and real members of the school, parish or community they represent. Send an official letter from the university, parish or community that lists the choir members' names.","A choir has 16 to 24 singers and one conductor. Other instrumentalists needed in a piece must come from within the choir.","Members may sing with only one group at all levels. The conductor may perform with another group only in another class.","Every round: a well-balanced free program of a cappella pieces with contrasting styles, language and time period. The video elimination must be a live recording (not a virtual choir), with no technical changes to the sound, an introduction of the choir's name, the conductor's name and the titles and composers or arrangers, and no cuts.","National Finals: include at least one piece by a composer who is alive at the time of submission (Filipino or not) and not sung before. A contest piece is given out after the semifinals.","Pieces may not be repeated at any level.","The choir sings in the key written in the score.","Send PDF scores of the video elimination pieces with the general packet. The last date for pieces is 15 days before the date of the elimination, semifinal and final rounds. Pieces cannot be changed after submission.","The PDFs must have the permission of the composer or publisher, except for public domain pieces."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Three expert judges. Technical merit 50 percent and artistic merit 50 percent.","Technical: overall sound quality, steady intonation, accurate rhythm, width of dynamic range, correct harmony and proper diction.","Artistic: musicality (expression, interpretation and style, tone, balance and blend) and programming (choice of pieces, presentation, faithfulness to the score, variety, difficulty and suitability to the choir).","Time over the limit: 1 point for each minute. 1 to 30 seconds over is 0.5 point. More than 30 seconds is 1 full point."],"Points":["First, Second and Third prizes are given in the national finals. A prize may be left out if the jury finds the choirs below the technical and artistic standard.","The jury may give other special awards."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- 2025 edition: a group class for school, church, cultural, civic or community choirs, mixed or equal voices.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Video elimination: singing time up to 9 minutes (not counting entrance, pause and exit).\\n- Semifinal: up to 12 minutes.\\n- National Finals: up to 15 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Singers must be Filipino citizens, 18 to 30 years old by December 31, 2025, and real members of the school, parish or community they represent. Send an official letter from the university, parish or community that lists the choir members' names.\\n- A choir has 16 to 24 singers and one conductor. Other instrumentalists needed in a piece must come from within the choir.\\n- Members may sing with only one group at all levels. The conductor may perform with another group only in another class.\\n- Every round: a well-balanced free program of a cappella pieces with contrasting styles, language and time period. The video elimination must be a live recording (not a virtual choir), with no technical changes to the sound, an introduction of the choir's name, the conductor's name and the titles and composers or arrangers, and no cuts.\\n- National Finals: include at least one piece by a composer who is alive at the time of submission (Filipino or not) and not sung before. A contest piece is given out after the semifinals.\\n- Pieces may not be repeated at any level.\\n- The choir sings in the key written in the score.\\n- Send PDF scores of the video elimination pieces with the general packet. The last date for pieces is 15 days before the date of the elimination, semifinal and final rounds. Pieces cannot be changed after submission.\\n- The PDFs must have the permission of the composer or publisher, except for public domain pieces.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Three expert judges. Technical merit 50 percent and artistic merit 50 percent.\\n- Technical: overall sound quality, steady intonation, accurate rhythm, width of dynamic range, correct harmony and proper diction.\\n- Artistic: musicality (expression, interpretation and style, tone, balance and blend) and programming (choice of pieces, presentation, faithfulness to the score, variety, difficulty and suitability to the choir).\\n- Time over the limit: 1 point for each minute. 1 to 30 seconds over is 0.5 point. More than 30 seconds is 1 full point.\\n\\n## Points\\n- First, Second and Third prizes are given in the national finals. A prize may be left out if the jury finds the choirs below the technical and artistic standard.\\n- The jury may give other special awards."},{"Title":"Symphonic Band","Source":"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Symphonic Band","Sections":{"About":["2025 edition: a group class for symphonic bands of an educational institution, church, civic, religious or cultural organisation or community."],"TimeAndFormat":["Video elimination: total playing time 15 to 20 minutes.","Semifinal: total playing time up to 35 minutes.","National Finals: total playing time 35 to 45 minutes, from the start of the first piece to the cut-off of the last piece. 5 points are deducted for each minute or part of a minute under or over."],"Rules":["Members must be Filipino citizens, not more than 23 years old by December 31, 2025. The Conductor and the Assistant Conductor are exempt from the age rule.","The band has 45 to 60 players, one Conductor and one Assistant Conductor.","Conductors and players may perform with one group only at all levels.","Awards in other local or international band competitions have no bearing on NAMCYA standards. Bands that won before may enter if they follow all rules.","Composition: clarinet (1, 2, 3), piccolo and flute (1, 2), oboe and English horn (optional), alto sax (1, 2), tenor sax, baritone sax (optional), bassoon (optional), trumpet and cornet (1, 2, 3), French horn (1 to 4), trombone (1, 2, 3), euphonium, tuba and sousaphone, timpani and percussion.","Video elimination: an overture from the Classical, Romantic or 20th and 21st century era, transcribed and published for symphonic band (not Tchaikovsky's 1812 Overture, Marche Slave or Festival Overture on the Danish National Anthem, Op. 15; one movement of a symphony may be accepted), and a concert march that is an original work for symphonic band.","Semifinal: the same overture and march, and a contemporary original work for symphonic band by a living composer.","National Finals: the same overture, march and contemporary work. The instrumentation of the scores must be strictly followed.","Documented permission from living composers and music publishers is strictly required.","Send PDF scores with the general packet. Each title page shows the name of the band and the level (Eliminations, Semi-Finals or Finals). Send one clear copy of the NSO-issued birth certificate of the conductor and of each band member.","Incomplete or missing submission, or falsification, of these requirements is a valid reason for disqualification.","A change of members after the application packet is allowed only in writing by the Conductor, received by the NAMCYA office within seven calendar days after the semifinals the band played in. The band must be a qualified finalist, the change applies only to the National Finals, and at most five changes are allowed in all.","The request goes with one copy of the substitute's NSO-issued birth certificate and a revised list of members with all signatures, addressed to the Chairman of the Symphonic Band Competition and emailed to the NAMCYA applications email. The Chairman replies and the Conductor is told.","Substitutions without approval are strictly forbidden and may lead to disqualification of the band.","Suggested repertoire: overtures such as Egmont and Leonore (Beethoven), Semiramide and William Tell (Rossini), Poet and Peasant and Light Cavalry (Suppe), Sicilian Vespers and La Forza del Destino (Verdi), Rienzi and Flying Dutchman (Wagner), Oberon and Der Freischutz (Weber).","Suggested contemporary works: Celebration Fanfare, Faith of the Gods and Portrait of Freedom (Steven Reineke), Orient Express and Hanover Festival (Philip Sparke), and original band works by Robert Smith, Frank Tichelli, James Barnes, Samuel Hazo, Richard Saucedo, Michael Sweeney, David Holsinger, James Swearingen, John Williams and others of the same level. Works by Filipino and other Asian composers of the same level are encouraged.","Marches that are used in the field and not written only for concert performance are not accepted."],"Allowed":["Choreography and movements that are part of the basic structure of a piece (hand clapping, foot stomping, body percussion) if the score of the composer or arranger clearly shows them."],"NotAllowed":["Electronic instruments. Only non-electronic instruments are allowed.","A recorded minus-one. Electronically produced sounds are allowed only if they are part of the original score.","Marks that show a school or a residence on the attire."],"Judging":["The judges consider the level of difficulty of the pieces played."],"Points":["Only one winner is announced as Champion. For an exceptional non-winner, at most two Honorable Mention awards are given."],"Notes":["Attire must be simple and presentable, with no identifying marks such as school or residence signs."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- 2025 edition: a group class for symphonic bands of an educational institution, church, civic, religious or cultural organisation or community.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Video elimination: total playing time 15 to 20 minutes.\\n- Semifinal: total playing time up to 35 minutes.\\n- National Finals: total playing time 35 to 45 minutes, from the start of the first piece to the cut-off of the last piece. 5 points are deducted for each minute or part of a minute under or over.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Members must be Filipino citizens, not more than 23 years old by December 31, 2025. The Conductor and the Assistant Conductor are exempt from the age rule.\\n- The band has 45 to 60 players, one Conductor and one Assistant Conductor.\\n- Conductors and players may perform with one group only at all levels.\\n- Awards in other local or international band competitions have no bearing on NAMCYA standards. Bands that won before may enter if they follow all rules.\\n- Composition: clarinet (1, 2, 3), piccolo and flute (1, 2), oboe and English horn (optional), alto sax (1, 2), tenor sax, baritone sax (optional), bassoon (optional), trumpet and cornet (1, 2, 3), French horn (1 to 4), trombone (1, 2, 3), euphonium, tuba and sousaphone, timpani and percussion.\\n- Video elimination: an overture from the Classical, Romantic or 20th and 21st century era, transcribed and published for symphonic band (not Tchaikovsky's 1812 Overture, Marche Slave or Festival Overture on the Danish National Anthem, Op. 15; one movement of a symphony may be accepted), and a concert march that is an original work for symphonic band.\\n- Semifinal: the same overture and march, and a contemporary original work for symphonic band by a living composer.\\n- National Finals: the same overture, march and contemporary work. The instrumentation of the scores must be strictly followed.\\n- Documented permission from living composers and music publishers is strictly required.\\n- Send PDF scores with the general packet. Each title page shows the name of the band and the level (Eliminations, Semi-Finals or Finals). Send one clear copy of the NSO-issued birth certificate of the conductor and of each band member.\\n- Incomplete or missing submission, or falsification, of these requirements is a valid reason for disqualification.\\n- A change of members after the application packet is allowed only in writing by the Conductor, received by the NAMCYA office within seven calendar days after the semifinals the band played in. The band must be a qualified finalist, the change applies only to the National Finals, and at most five changes are allowed in all.\\n- The request goes with one copy of the substitute's NSO-issued birth certificate and a revised list of members with all signatures, addressed to the Chairman of the Symphonic Band Competition and emailed to the NAMCYA applications email. The Chairman replies and the Conductor is told.\\n- Substitutions without approval are strictly forbidden and may lead to disqualification of the band.\\n- Suggested repertoire: overtures such as Egmont and Leonore (Beethoven), Semiramide and William Tell (Rossini), Poet and Peasant and Light Cavalry (Suppe), Sicilian Vespers and La Forza del Destino (Verdi), Rienzi and Flying Dutchman (Wagner), Oberon and Der Freischutz (Weber).\\n- Suggested contemporary works: Celebration Fanfare, Faith of the Gods and Portrait of Freedom (Steven Reineke), Orient Express and Hanover Festival (Philip Sparke), and original band works by Robert Smith, Frank Tichelli, James Barnes, Samuel Hazo, Richard Saucedo, Michael Sweeney, David Holsinger, James Swearingen, John Williams and others of the same level. Works by Filipino and other Asian composers of the same level are encouraged.\\n- Marches that are used in the field and not written only for concert performance are not accepted.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Choreography and movements that are part of the basic structure of a piece (hand clapping, foot stomping, body percussion) if the score of the composer or arranger clearly shows them.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Electronic instruments. Only non-electronic instruments are allowed.\\n- A recorded minus-one. Electronically produced sounds are allowed only if they are part of the original score.\\n- Marks that show a school or a residence on the attire.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the level of difficulty of the pieces played.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Only one winner is announced as Champion. For an exceptional non-winner, at most two Honorable Mention awards are given.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Attire must be simple and presentable, with no identifying marks such as school or residence signs."},{"Title":"Senior Piano","Source":"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Senior Piano","Sections":{"About":["2025 edition: a solo piano class."],"TimeAndFormat":["Video elimination: up to 20 minutes.","Semifinal: a full solo recital of at least 45 minutes and not more than 60 minutes, without repetition."],"Rules":["Video elimination: one Prelude and Fugue by J.S. Bach, one virtuosic etude, and one nocturne.","Semifinal: one Baroque work, one complete Classical sonata, one Romantic work and one 20th or 21st century work.","National Finals: a complete concerto and a contest piece (announced after the video elimination round).","Pieces played in earlier rounds may not be repeated in later rounds. The nocturne used in the elimination round is not allowed in any later round.","Piano works may differ in length to meet the time of each round.","In the video, the face and hands must be visible at all times."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- 2025 edition: a solo piano class.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Video elimination: up to 20 minutes.\\n- Semifinal: a full solo recital of at least 45 minutes and not more than 60 minutes, without repetition.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Video elimination: one Prelude and Fugue by J.S. Bach, one virtuosic etude, and one nocturne.\\n- Semifinal: one Baroque work, one complete Classical sonata, one Romantic work and one 20th or 21st century work.\\n- National Finals: a complete concerto and a contest piece (announced after the video elimination round).\\n- Pieces played in earlier rounds may not be repeated in later rounds. The nocturne used in the elimination round is not allowed in any later round.\\n- Piano works may differ in length to meet the time of each round.\\n- In the video, the face and hands must be visible at all times."},{"Title":"Senior Strings (Violin)","Source":"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Senior Strings","Sections":{"About":["2025 edition: a solo strings class. Violin has its own repertoire list. Violin and the lower strings go on in separate groups: up to 12 candidates after the elimination and up to 6 after the semifinal."],"TimeAndFormat":["Semifinal: a live round with a 30 to 45 minute performance.","Total times are strictly enforced and include any pause between pieces. Repeats are the performer's choice. Cutting long piano accompaniment parts with taste is encouraged."],"Rules":["Choose a balanced program that shows versatility. The chamber music piece and the concerto must be of different periods or styles.","Modern concertos and show pieces, chamber music and the obligatory contest piece may be played with the sheet music. The other pieces are memorized. A fully memorized program is preferred.","Pieces not in the recommended repertoire list are allowed if they are of the same or higher level. Send a written request to the Chairperson of the Strings Competition through the NAMCYA office.","After you submit, the repertoire list may be changed only once, by a written request signed by the contestant to the Chairperson of the Strings Competition through the NAMCYA office at least 10 working days before the live rounds. Send a clear scan of the new score.","Elimination round: no more than 12 candidates from the upper strings and 12 from the lower strings go on. Play the first movement of the concerto that you will play in the National Finals.","Semifinal (live): no more than 6 candidates from the upper strings and 6 from the lower strings go on. Play, in any order that fits the program, a J.S. Bach selection, a Filipino piece, contrasting movements of a duo chamber work and a virtuoso, concert or show piece.","Final (live): the complete concerto (the elimination entry) and the obligatory contest piece (to be announced). The contest piece may only be played at the NAMCYA 2025 string finals and its sheet music may not be shared.","Recommended violin list, Bach: sets from the Sonatas and Partitas BWV 1001 to 1006 (memorized). Chamber music: violin and piano sonatas by Bartok, Beethoven, Brahms, Debussy, Grieg, Mozart, Prokofiev, Ravel, Schumann (Op. 105 or 121), Strauss, Shostakovich or equivalent. Concertos (memorized): Barber, Beethoven, Brahms, Bruch, Buenaventura, Dvorak, Glazunov, Haydn, Khachaturian, Lalo, Mendelssohn, Mozart 4 or 5, Paganini 1 or 2, San Pedro, Saint-Saens 3, Sibelius, Tchaikovsky, Vieuxtemps 4 or 5, Wieniawski.","Recommended violin list, Filipino art music: any selection from the Romero or Kabayao sets of Filipino songs, any earlier NAMCYA contest piece, or any art music by a Filipino composer (agree with the Strings Chair). Concert and show pieces: Bazzini, Beethoven Romance Op. 50, Chopin, Dinicu, Elgar, Kreisler, Kroll, Paganini, Ravel Tzigane, Sarasate, Saint-Saens, Tchaikovsky, Vitali, Wieniawski, Ysaye or equivalent.","Video: record with one camera on a tripod in horizontal position, MP4 preferred. The face, both arms, the entire bow and the instrument must be seen. The instrument must be tuned or the video is disqualified. Wear presentable attire. Record the video for the competition, date stamped not earlier than March 7, 2025. Show a full performance of the chosen repertoire with no cuts, editing, zooming, panning or audio enhancement.","The order of performances is set by drawing lots and stays the same through the competition.","You bring your own accompanist and your own instrument, and you get the performing rights for your pieces.","You may not speak to the judges during the competition.","First place winners may not join the same class in the following year.","Not following, or falsifying, a requirement is a sufficient ground for disqualification.","Live events strictly follow IATF regulations and may change."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The final decisions of the jury cannot be reversed."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- 2025 edition: a solo strings class. Violin has its own repertoire list. Violin and the lower strings go on in separate groups: up to 12 candidates after the elimination and up to 6 after the semifinal.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Semifinal: a live round with a 30 to 45 minute performance.\\n- Total times are strictly enforced and include any pause between pieces. Repeats are the performer's choice. Cutting long piano accompaniment parts with taste is encouraged.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Choose a balanced program that shows versatility. The chamber music piece and the concerto must be of different periods or styles.\\n- Modern concertos and show pieces, chamber music and the obligatory contest piece may be played with the sheet music. The other pieces are memorized. A fully memorized program is preferred.\\n- Pieces not in the recommended repertoire list are allowed if they are of the same or higher level. Send a written request to the Chairperson of the Strings Competition through the NAMCYA office.\\n- After you submit, the repertoire list may be changed only once, by a written request signed by the contestant to the Chairperson of the Strings Competition through the NAMCYA office at least 10 working days before the live rounds. Send a clear scan of the new score.\\n- Elimination round: no more than 12 candidates from the upper strings and 12 from the lower strings go on. Play the first movement of the concerto that you will play in the National Finals.\\n- Semifinal (live): no more than 6 candidates from the upper strings and 6 from the lower strings go on. Play, in any order that fits the program, a J.S. Bach selection, a Filipino piece, contrasting movements of a duo chamber work and a virtuoso, concert or show piece.\\n- Final (live): the complete concerto (the elimination entry) and the obligatory contest piece (to be announced). The contest piece may only be played at the NAMCYA 2025 string finals and its sheet music may not be shared.\\n- Recommended violin list, Bach: sets from the Sonatas and Partitas BWV 1001 to 1006 (memorized). Chamber music: violin and piano sonatas by Bartok, Beethoven, Brahms, Debussy, Grieg, Mozart, Prokofiev, Ravel, Schumann (Op. 105 or 121), Strauss, Shostakovich or equivalent. Concertos (memorized): Barber, Beethoven, Brahms, Bruch, Buenaventura, Dvorak, Glazunov, Haydn, Khachaturian, Lalo, Mendelssohn, Mozart 4 or 5, Paganini 1 or 2, San Pedro, Saint-Saens 3, Sibelius, Tchaikovsky, Vieuxtemps 4 or 5, Wieniawski.\\n- Recommended violin list, Filipino art music: any selection from the Romero or Kabayao sets of Filipino songs, any earlier NAMCYA contest piece, or any art music by a Filipino composer (agree with the Strings Chair). Concert and show pieces: Bazzini, Beethoven Romance Op. 50, Chopin, Dinicu, Elgar, Kreisler, Kroll, Paganini, Ravel Tzigane, Sarasate, Saint-Saens, Tchaikovsky, Vitali, Wieniawski, Ysaye or equivalent.\\n- Video: record with one camera on a tripod in horizontal position, MP4 preferred. The face, both arms, the entire bow and the instrument must be seen. The instrument must be tuned or the video is disqualified. Wear presentable attire. Record the video for the competition, date stamped not earlier than March 7, 2025. Show a full performance of the chosen repertoire with no cuts, editing, zooming, panning or audio enhancement.\\n- The order of performances is set by drawing lots and stays the same through the competition.\\n- You bring your own accompanist and your own instrument, and you get the performing rights for your pieces.\\n- You may not speak to the judges during the competition.\\n- First place winners may not join the same class in the following year.\\n- Not following, or falsifying, a requirement is a sufficient ground for disqualification.\\n- Live events strictly follow IATF regulations and may change.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The final decisions of the jury cannot be reversed."},{"Title":"Senior Lower Strings (Viola, Cello, Double Bass)","Source":"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Senior Strings","Sections":{"About":["2025 edition: a solo class for viola, cello and double bass (contrabass), with the same rules as Senior Strings. Lower strings candidates go on in a separate group: up to 12 after the elimination and up to 6 after the semifinal."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Follow the Senior Strings rules (rounds, recital program, video rules, repertoire changes, accompanist, instrument, contest piece, drawing of lots and disqualification).","Bach selection, viola (memorized): the Sonatas and Partitas sets transcribed for viola, or Cello Suites BWV 1007 to 1012 (Suites 1 to 4: a prelude and 2 dances; Suites 5 and 6: a prelude and a dance).","Bach selection, cello and contrabass (memorized): Cello Suites BWV 1007 to 1012 in the same way.","Viola chamber music and concertos include Bax, Beethoven, Brahms Op. 120, Clarke, Franck, Glinka, Hindemith, Hummel, Schubert Arpeggione, Shostakovich Op. 147 and Vieuxtemps; concertos by Forsyth, Hoffmeister, Mozart No. 3 (transcribed), Stamitz, Schubert and Zelter. The full cello and contrabass lists are printed in the 2025 category guidelines.","Filipino art music: for viola, Hating Gabi and Cavatina; for cello, Cavatina and the Romances by Abelardo, Buenaventura and Molina; for contrabass, Angel Pena and Agot Espino (Kundiman ng Langit). Any earlier NAMCYA contest piece or any art music by a Filipino composer is also allowed."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- 2025 edition: a solo class for viola, cello and double bass (contrabass), with the same rules as Senior Strings. Lower strings candidates go on in a separate group: up to 12 after the elimination and up to 6 after the semifinal.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Follow the Senior Strings rules (rounds, recital program, video rules, repertoire changes, accompanist, instrument, contest piece, drawing of lots and disqualification).\\n- Bach selection, viola (memorized): the Sonatas and Partitas sets transcribed for viola, or Cello Suites BWV 1007 to 1012 (Suites 1 to 4: a prelude and 2 dances; Suites 5 and 6: a prelude and a dance).\\n- Bach selection, cello and contrabass (memorized): Cello Suites BWV 1007 to 1012 in the same way.\\n- Viola chamber music and concertos include Bax, Beethoven, Brahms Op. 120, Clarke, Franck, Glinka, Hindemith, Hummel, Schubert Arpeggione, Shostakovich Op. 147 and Vieuxtemps; concertos by Forsyth, Hoffmeister, Mozart No. 3 (transcribed), Stamitz, Schubert and Zelter. The full cello and contrabass lists are printed in the 2025 category guidelines.\\n- Filipino art music: for viola, Hating Gabi and Cavatina; for cello, Cavatina and the Romances by Abelardo, Buenaventura and Molina; for contrabass, Angel Pena and Agot Espino (Kundiman ng Langit). Any earlier NAMCYA contest piece or any art music by a Filipino composer is also allowed."},{"Title":"Senior Voice","Source":"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Senior Voice","Sections":{"About":["2025 edition: a solo voice class split into Senior Voice A (ages 19 to 24) and Senior Voice B (ages 25 to 31)."],"TimeAndFormat":["Video elimination: one aria and two songs from the submitted repertoire, no more than 12 minutes in all.","Semifinal: three pieces from the submitted repertoire that were not sung in the elimination, no more than 12 minutes in all.","Final: a 15 to 20 minute program from the submitted repertoire, including the contest piece."],"Rules":["There is no division by voice type (soprano, alto, tenor, bass). All competitors in a sub-category compete for the same prizes.","Prepare the submitted repertoire: two arias from opera, operetta, oratorio or cantata, in the original language and key and in contrasting styles; three art songs in at least two different languages (Italian, French, Spanish, German or English), sung in the original language, with transposition allowed; two songs by a Filipino composer; and the contest piece (announced after the video elimination round).","For operas translated and reworked by the composer (as in some works of Rossini and Donizetti), the competitor may choose the language. Arias are sung with the recitative or cabaletta or cavatina, if present. Filipino arias may be included.","The Filipino songs are art songs (including Kundiman and Kumintang) or transcriptions of folk songs for solo voice and piano. At least one song must be in a Filipino language. The second may be in any language that the music was set to."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Senior Voice A and Senior Voice B each: First Prize with a cash award and a trophy, Second Prize with a trophy, Third Prize with a trophy."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- 2025 edition: a solo voice class split into Senior Voice A (ages 19 to 24) and Senior Voice B (ages 25 to 31).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Video elimination: one aria and two songs from the submitted repertoire, no more than 12 minutes in all.\\n- Semifinal: three pieces from the submitted repertoire that were not sung in the elimination, no more than 12 minutes in all.\\n- Final: a 15 to 20 minute program from the submitted repertoire, including the contest piece.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- There is no division by voice type (soprano, alto, tenor, bass). All competitors in a sub-category compete for the same prizes.\\n- Prepare the submitted repertoire: two arias from opera, operetta, oratorio or cantata, in the original language and key and in contrasting styles; three art songs in at least two different languages (Italian, French, Spanish, German or English), sung in the original language, with transposition allowed; two songs by a Filipino composer; and the contest piece (announced after the video elimination round).\\n- For operas translated and reworked by the composer (as in some works of Rossini and Donizetti), the competitor may choose the language. Arias are sung with the recitative or cabaletta or cavatina, if present. Filipino arias may be included.\\n- The Filipino songs are art songs (including Kundiman and Kumintang) or transcriptions of folk songs for solo voice and piano. At least one song must be in a Filipino language. The second may be in any language that the music was set to.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Senior Voice A and Senior Voice B each: First Prize with a cash award and a trophy, Second Prize with a trophy, Third Prize with a trophy."},{"Title":"Woodwinds (Open)","Source":"NAMCYA 2025 category guidelines Woodwinds (Open)","Sections":{"About":["2025 edition: a solo class for flute, clarinet, oboe, bassoon and saxophone."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Video elimination: flute, clarinet, oboe and bassoon play the 1st and 2nd movements of a Mozart concerto, with the cadenza if there is one. Saxophone plays two contrasting movements (slow and fast) of a sonata or concerto, with the cadenza if there is one.","Semifinal: a complete sonata from the Romantic period to the present, not played in the video elimination round. Saxophone plays a piece different from the video elimination round.","National Finals: a complete concerto from the Classical period to the present, and a contest piece (announced after the video elimination round)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- 2025 edition: a solo class for flute, clarinet, oboe, bassoon and saxophone.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Video elimination: flute, clarinet, oboe and bassoon play the 1st and 2nd movements of a Mozart concerto, with the cadenza if there is one. Saxophone plays two contrasting movements (slow and fast) of a sonata or concerto, with the cadenza if there is one.\\n- Semifinal: a complete sonata from the Romantic period to the present, not played in the video elimination round. Saxophone plays a piece different from the video elimination round.\\n- National Finals: a complete concerto from the Classical period to the present, and a contest piece (announced after the video elimination round)."},{"Title":"Traditional Music Expressions","Source":"NAMCYA 2026 Traditional Music Expressions guidelines","Sections":{"About":["This is the audition for the NAMCYA Traditional Music Expressions Showcase. It features live performances of traditional expressive forms of local communities in the Philippines. Theme for 2026: {{TMETheme}}.","A traditional expressive form is performed in everyday life or at special events in the community and is part of its living heritage and identity. A performance may include singing, speech, instruments, body movement, materials and traditional attire.","NAMCYA wants young members of the community to learn and nurture their living heritage, so each group must prominently feature one or more young members."],"TimeAndFormat":["The performance is up to 15 minutes, including the entrance and exit from the stage."],"Rules":["Performers, individual or group, may come from any local community in the Philippines (indigenous, lowland, Christian or urban). They may be existing performers or groups from a school, church, family or community.","Each performance must prominently feature at least one member who is no more than 18 years old on {{AgeCutoffDate}}.","A contingent has up to 17 members. One of them is the local expert who serves as the consultant and leader of the group.","The performance takes any one of these formats: an ensemble performance, a solo performance, or a mixed solo and ensemble performance (one or more pieces each).","Each performance is prepared under the guidance of a local expert on the expressive form (an elder, master, teacher, artist or local leader) named by the community, who is the informant or consultant.","The group pays all travel costs to and from the Traditional Music Expressions Showcase in National Finals Week in Manila.","Keep the traditional way of performing as it is done in the community, including movements, materials and traditional attire. Mastery of musical skill is the main selection criterion, not theatre.","Performers bring their own costumes, instruments and other materials.","Audition requirements: the application form, an audio-video recording, and a written description with the titles of the pieces, a general description (up to 150 words), the instruments, other materials used, the text in the original language with a line-by-line translation into Filipino or English (if it applies), and a short biographical note (up to 250 words) of the local expert with name, community of origin, training history and other credentials.","Recording: use a space the shape and size of a live stage, with good light (daytime or natural outdoor light is best) and little noise (no passing vehicles, fans, air conditioners or loud animal or human sounds). Avoid places with echo such as churches or gymnasiums. An external microphone near the performers is advised if the camera microphone is weak.","The recording starts with an announcement of the group's name and the titles of the pieces as in the application form, then the performance as it would be in the Showcase in National Finals Week in November 2026.","Shoot from the angle of the audience, far enough to show the whole performance area and near enough to see the faces. Put the camera on a tripod. Record continuously, without pausing or stopping."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Fire and live animals in the performance. You may use props for these parts of the expressive form.","Zoom or pan shots, editing, visual or audio enhancement, and pre-recorded music in the audition recording."],"Judging":["Musical skill 30 percent.","Interpretation 30 percent.","Cultural or musical significance of the repertoire 20 percent.","Transmission: the extent that the youth are featured in the performance, 20 percent."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Clothes inspired by culture are encouraged."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- This is the audition for the NAMCYA Traditional Music Expressions Showcase. It features live performances of traditional expressive forms of local communities in the Philippines. Theme for 2026: {{TMETheme}}.\\n- A traditional expressive form is performed in everyday life or at special events in the community and is part of its living heritage and identity. A performance may include singing, speech, instruments, body movement, materials and traditional attire.\\n- NAMCYA wants young members of the community to learn and nurture their living heritage, so each group must prominently feature one or more young members.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The performance is up to 15 minutes, including the entrance and exit from the stage.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Performers, individual or group, may come from any local community in the Philippines (indigenous, lowland, Christian or urban). They may be existing performers or groups from a school, church, family or community.\\n- Each performance must prominently feature at least one member who is no more than 18 years old on {{AgeCutoffDate}}.\\n- A contingent has up to 17 members. One of them is the local expert who serves as the consultant and leader of the group.\\n- The performance takes any one of these formats: an ensemble performance, a solo performance, or a mixed solo and ensemble performance (one or more pieces each).\\n- Each performance is prepared under the guidance of a local expert on the expressive form (an elder, master, teacher, artist or local leader) named by the community, who is the informant or consultant.\\n- The group pays all travel costs to and from the Traditional Music Expressions Showcase in National Finals Week in Manila.\\n- Keep the traditional way of performing as it is done in the community, including movements, materials and traditional attire. Mastery of musical skill is the main selection criterion, not theatre.\\n- Performers bring their own costumes, instruments and other materials.\\n- Audition requirements: the application form, an audio-video recording, and a written description with the titles of the pieces, a general description (up to 150 words), the instruments, other materials used, the text in the original language with a line-by-line translation into Filipino or English (if it applies), and a short biographical note (up to 250 words) of the local expert with name, community of origin, training history and other credentials.\\n- Recording: use a space the shape and size of a live stage, with good light (daytime or natural outdoor light is best) and little noise (no passing vehicles, fans, air conditioners or loud animal or human sounds). Avoid places with echo such as churches or gymnasiums. An external microphone near the performers is advised if the camera microphone is weak.\\n- The recording starts with an announcement of the group's name and the titles of the pieces as in the application form, then the performance as it would be in the Showcase in National Finals Week in November 2026.\\n- Shoot from the angle of the audience, far enough to show the whole performance area and near enough to see the faces. Put the camera on a tripod. Record continuously, without pausing or stopping.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Fire and live animals in the performance. You may use props for these parts of the expressive form.\\n- Zoom or pan shots, editing, visual or audio enhancement, and pre-recorded music in the audition recording.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Musical skill 30 percent.\\n- Interpretation 30 percent.\\n- Cultural or musical significance of the repertoire 20 percent.\\n- Transmission: the extent that the youth are featured in the performance, 20 percent.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Clothes inspired by culture are encouraged."}]`),r=[],s=[{Key:"AgeCutoffDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date on which ages are counted (2026 edition)",Value:"2026-12-31",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines and 2026 category guidelines (by December 31, 2026)"},{Key:"IntentToJoinWindow",Kind:"date",Label:"Intent-to-join form window",Value:"April 30 to May 7, 2026",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline"},{Key:"ApplicationDocsDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date for application documents",Value:"2026-05-08",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline"},{Key:"VideoScoresDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date for audition video and music scores (all classes except Traditional Music Expressions)",Value:"2026-05-22",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline"},{Key:"TMEVideoDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date for the Traditional Music Expressions audition video",Value:"2026-06-15",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline"},{Key:"VideoDateStampFrom",Kind:"date",Label:"Earliest date stamp allowed on an audition video",Value:"2026-01-26",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines VI 2b (date stamp not earlier than January 26, 2026)"},{Key:"EliminationRoundDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Video elimination round (via Zoom)",Value:"June 8-12, 2026",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline; X b"},{Key:"TMEEliminationDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Traditional Music Expressions video elimination round (via Zoom)",Value:"2026-07-18",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline"},{Key:"MindanaoSemifinal",Kind:"text",Label:"Mindanao Cluster semifinal round",Value:"August 28-29, 2026, Koronadal, South Cotabato",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline"},{Key:"VisayasSemifinal",Kind:"text",Label:"Visayas Cluster semifinal round",Value:"September 4-5, 2026, Tagbilaran, Bohol",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline"},{Key:"NorthernLuzonSemifinal",Kind:"text",Label:"Northern Luzon Cluster semifinal round",Value:"September 11-12, 2026, Don Mariano Marcos Memorial State University, Agoo, La Union",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline"},{Key:"SouthernLuzonSemifinal",Kind:"text",Label:"Southern Luzon Cluster semifinal round",Value:"September 18-19, 2026, Sorsogon City",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline"},{Key:"NCRSemifinal",Kind:"text",Label:"National Capital Region Cluster semifinal round",Value:"September 25-26, 2026, venue to be announced",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline"},{Key:"SoloSemifinals",Kind:"text",Label:"Solo semifinals",Value:"October 5-9, 2026, venue to be announced",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline"},{Key:"NationalFinalsDates",Kind:"date",Label:"National Finals Week",Value:"November 17-22, 2026",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline"},{Key:"FinalsVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"National Finals venue",Value:{Name:"The Metropolitan Theater",Address:"",City:"Metro Manila",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline; VIII 1 (Finals held in Metro Manila venues)"},{Key:"SecretariatAddress",Kind:"address",Label:"NAMCYA office",Value:{Name:"National Music Competitions for Young Artists Foundation Inc.",Address:"National Museum of the Philippines, Anthropology Building, P. Burgos Drive, Rizal Park",City:"Ermita, Philippines",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines cover page"},{Key:"SoloFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Registration fee, solo class",Value:"P1,500 per solo class entry, non-refundable (Philippine pesos)",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines VI 4 Fees"},{Key:"GroupFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Registration fee, group class",Value:"P2,500 per group class entry, non-refundable (Philippine pesos), including Senior Group Rondalla",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines VI 4 Fees"},{Key:"ApplicationsEmail",Kind:"contact",Label:"Email for technical issues, repertoire changes and all inquiries",Value:{Name:"NAMCYA Secretariat",Role:"Technical issues, change requests and inquiries",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"namcyainfo2026@gmail.com"},Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines VI 5d-e; VII d-e"},{Key:"SecretariatContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"NAMCYA office contact",Value:{Name:"NAMCYA Secretariat",Role:"General inquiries",Phone:"+63 949 9932592",WhatsApp:"",Email:"info@namcya.com"},Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines cover page (Fb.com/NAMCYAPH, +63 949 9932592, info@namcya.com, www.namcya.com)"},{Key:"OrganiserWebsite",Kind:"link",Label:"Organiser website",Value:"https://www.namcya.com",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines cover page"},{Key:"OrganiserFacebook",Kind:"link",Label:"Organiser Facebook page",Value:"https://www.facebook.com/NAMCYAPH",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines cover page (Fb.com/NAMCYAPH)"},{Key:"TMETheme",Kind:"text",Label:"Traditional Music Expressions theme (2026)",Value:"DALOY",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 Traditional Music Expressions guidelines title"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"News printed in the 2026 guidelines",Value:[{Date:"2026-01-26",Title:"Announcement of the 2026 categories",Text:"The 2026 categories were announced by social media posting on January 26, 2026.",Url:""},{Date:"",Title:"Dates and venues may change",Text:"Certain competition dates and venues are tentative. The NAMCYA Secretariat will release official updates if anything changes.",Url:""},{Date:"",Title:"After you submit",Text:"After you submit the intent-to-join form, you receive a confirmation and detailed instructions, and a Google Drive link to upload your videos, scores and other requirements. When your submission is complete, you receive a certificate that your entry is accepted for adjudication.",Url:""}],Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines V Timeline notes"}],l=[{Claim:"2026 rules, timeline, fees, application steps, awards and conduct: NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines (15 pages) for the 53rd NAMCYA Padayaw 2026, with the 2026 category guidelines, linked from the organiser's own Linktree.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own guidelines",Source:"NAMCYA 2026 General Guidelines and Traditional Music Expressions guidelines (NAMCYA Foundation)",Url:"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Kzz7WvnTwrxtE6-TJj3hcyoOhECzuWoQ/view"},{Claim:"The organiser's website page for 2026 links to the Linktree with the 2026 guidelines and category guidelines.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own website",Source:"NAMCYA website, 2026 NAMCYA Competitions and Guidelines",Url:"https://www.namcya.com/comptetition/2026-namcya-competitions-and-guidelines/"},{Claim:"Rules of the template's own classes (age limits, rounds, repertoire, group sizes, judging and awards) are from the 2025 General Guidelines and 2025 category guidelines (37 pages), because the 2026 edition replaced the class list.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own guidelines (previous edition)",Source:"NAMCYA 2025 General Guidelines and category guidelines",Url:"https://www.namcya.com/comptetition/2026-namcya-competitions-and-guidelines/"}],d={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:n,Page:o,ParticipantTypes:i,AgeGroups:t,Competitions:a,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:s,Evidence:l};export{t as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,a as Competitions,l as Evidence,n as Note,o as Page,i as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,c as Year,d as default};
